   "source": [
    "# Member 2 — Autonomous Navigation & Replanning\n",
    "\n",
    "## 1. Partial-Observation Problem\n",
    "\n",
    "In a partially observable maze, the robot does not know the complete maze at the beginning. It observes its surroundings while moving and gradually builds a discovered map.\n",
    "\n",
    "The robot updates its knowledge whenever new information is obtained. If a newly discovered obstacle affects the current path, the robot updates the map and replans the path to the goal.\n",
    "\n",
    "The navigation process is:\n",
    "\n",
    "**Start → Observe → Update Map → Plan Path → Move → Observe Again → Replan if Required**\n",
    "\n",
    "## 2. Ground-Truth Map and Discovered Map\n",
    "\n",
    "The **ground-truth map** represents the complete maze generated by the maze generator. It contains all walls, free cells, the start position and the goal.\n",
    "\n",
    "The **discovered map** represents only the information currently known by the robot. Cells that have not been observed remain unknown.\n",
    "\n",
    "Cell representation:\n",
    "\n",
    "- `?` = Unknown cell\n",
    "- `.` = Free cell\n",
    "- `#` = Wall\n",
    "- `S` = Start\n",
    "- `G` = Goal\n",
    "\n",
    "The ground-truth map contains complete information, while the discovered map is gradually updated as the robot explores the maze.\n",
    "\n",
    "## 3. Robot State\n",
    "\n",
    "The robot maintains the following information during navigation:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Current position\n",
    "- Goal position\n",
    "- Discovered map\n",
    "- Current planned path\n",
    "\n",
    "The robot state is updated whenever the robot moves or discovers new information.\n",
    "\n",
    "## 4. Observation Model\n",
    "\n",
    "The robot observes the neighbouring cells around its current position according to the observation model selected by the project team.\n",
    "\n",
    "The observation reveals whether nearby cells are free or blocked. Unknown cells remain unknown until they are observed.\n",
    "\n",
    "Observation is performed during navigation so that the discovered map can be updated as the robot moves.\n",
    "\n",
    "## 5. Robot Navigation Cycle\n",
    "\n",
    "The proposed navigation cycle is:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Start from the initial position.\n",
    "2. Observe the surrounding environment.\n",
    "3. Update the discovered map.\n",
    "4. Plan a path using the available information.\n",
    "5. Move along the planned path.\n",
    "6. Observe the surroundings again.\n",
    "7. Check whether new information has been discovered.\n",
    "8. If new information affects the current path, update the map and replan.\n",
    "9. Continue until the goal is reached or no valid path exists.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Navigation cycle:**\n",
    "\n",
    "**Start → Observe → Update Map → Plan → Move → Observe Again → Check for New Information → Replan if Required**\n",
    "\n",
    "## 6. Obstacle Discovery\n",
    "\n",
    "During navigation, the robot may discover an obstacle that was previously unknown.\n",
    "\n",
    "When a new obstacle is discovered:\n",
    "\n",
    "**New obstacle → Update discovered map → Check current path → Replan if path is affected**\n",
    "\n",
    "If the newly discovered wall blocks the current route, the previous path is no longer valid and a new path needs to be calculated.\n",
    "\n",
    "## 7. Reactive A*\n",
    "\n",
    "Reactive A* is a navigation approach where path planning can be repeated as the robot discovers new information.\n",
    "\n",
    "Initially, A* generates a path using the information currently available to the robot. The robot follows the path while observing the environment.\n",
    "\n",
    "If a newly discovered obstacle affects the current path, the discovered map is updated and A* is run again to obtain a new path.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Initial Map → A* → Initial Path → Robot Moves → New Obstacle → Update Map → Run A* Again → New Path**\n",
    "\n",
    "## 8. Replanning\n",
    "\n",
    "Replanning means calculating a new path when the robot's current planned route is affected by newly discovered information.\n",
    "\n",
    "The purpose of replanning is to allow the robot to adapt to the changing knowledge of the maze instead of continuing along an invalid route.\n",
    "\n",
    "## 9. Navigation Metrics\n",
    "\n",
    "The following metrics will be considered for autonomous navigation:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Metric | Description |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| Replan Count | Number of times a new path is calculated |\n",
    "| Path Length | Length of the resulting path |\n",
    "| Actual Distance Travelled | Total distance travelled by the robot |\n",
    "| Discovered Obstacles | Number of previously unknown obstacles discovered |\n",
    "| Execution Time | Time required for navigation and planning |\n",
    "\n",
    "## 10. Paper Study — Navigation Perspective\n",
    "\n",
    "For the selected research paper, the following navigation aspects are considered:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Environment or maze type\n",
    "- Robot assumptions\n",
    "- Available environmental information\n",
    "- Observation model\n",
    "- Obstacle discovery mechanism\n",
    "- Replanning strategy\n",
    "- Navigation/search algorithm\n",
    "- Performance metrics\n",
    "\n",
    "These aspects will be compared with the navigation approach used in our simulated maze environment.\n",
    "\n",
    "## 11. Initial Navigation Observations\n",
    "\n",
    "The following points will be investigated using the simulated experiments:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Whether every newly discovered obstacle requires replanning.\n",
    "2. Which maze structures result in more replans.\n",
    "3. Whether partial observation increases the distance travelled.\n",
    "4. How maze size affects the number of replans.\n",
    "5. Whether visually complex mazes always require more replanning.\n",
    "\n",
    "These observations will be finalized using the results obtained from the actual experiments.\n",
    "\n",
    "## 12. Navigation Design Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "The proposed navigation system allows the robot to operate without complete knowledge of the maze.\n",
    "\n",
    "The robot observes its surroundings, maintains a discovered map, plans a path using available information, moves through the maze, updates the map when new information is discovered, and replans whenever the current route is affected.\n",
    "\n",
    "This provides the foundation for implementing autonomous navigation and reactive replanning in later stages of the project."
   ]
