    "# Member 2 — Reactive Navigation Experimental Methodology\n",
    "\n",
    "## 13. Reactive A* Experimental Methodology\n",
    "\n",
    "The purpose of the experiment is to study how a robot can navigate a maze when the complete maze is not known initially.\n",
    "\n",
    "The robot starts with a partially known discovered map. It observes the environment while moving and updates the discovered map whenever new information is obtained.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Experimental Procedure\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Generate a maze using the existing maze generator.\n",
    "2. Keep the complete generated maze as the ground-truth map.\n",
    "3. Initialize the robot with a partially unknown discovered map.\n",
    "4. Set the robot at the start cell.\n",
    "5. Observe the neighbouring cells from the current position.\n",
    "6. Update the discovered map using the observation.\n",
    "7. Run A* on the currently discovered map.\n",
    "8. Move the robot along the planned path.\n",
    "9. Observe the environment again after movement.\n",
    "10. Check whether a newly discovered wall blocks or changes the current planned path.\n",
    "11. If the current path is affected, discard the affected path and run A* again.\n",
    "12. Continue this process until the robot reaches the goal or no valid path exists.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Reactive Navigation Flow\n",
    "\n",
    "Ground Truth Maze\n",
    "→ Partial Discovered Map\n",
    "→ Observe\n",
    "→ Update Discovered Map\n",
    "→ A* Planning\n",
    "→ Move\n",
    "→ Observe Again\n",
    "→ New Obstacle?\n",
    "→ Yes: Update Map → Replan with A*\n",
    "→ No: Continue\n",
    "→ Goal Reached\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 14. Obstacle Discovery and Replanning Condition\n",
    "\n",
    "A newly discovered obstacle does not always require replanning.\n",
    "\n",
    "Replanning is required when the newly discovered information affects the robot's current planned route.\n",
    "\n",
    "For example:\n",
    "\n",
    "- If a newly discovered wall is outside the current path, the robot can continue following the existing path.\n",
    "- If a newly discovered wall blocks a cell or connection required by the current path, the current path becomes invalid and A* must be executed again.\n",
    "- If the new information reveals that the current route is no longer optimal, replanning can also be performed.\n",
    "\n",
    "Therefore, the main replanning condition is:\n",
    "\n",
    "**New information + effect on current path → Replanning required**\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 15. Proposed Partial-Observation Experiment\n",
    "\n",
    "The experiment can compare navigation when the robot has complete information with navigation when the robot discovers the maze progressively.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Case A — Complete Map\n",
    "\n",
    "The robot receives the complete ground-truth maze before navigation.\n",
    "\n",
    "A* is executed using the complete map and the resulting path is followed to the goal.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Case B — Partial Observation\n",
    "\n",
    "The robot initially knows only the starting area and progressively discovers additional cells while moving.\n",
    "\n",
    "A* is repeatedly executed whenever newly discovered obstacles affect the current path.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Parameters to Record\n",
    "\n",
    "- Maze size\n",
    "- Start position\n",
    "- Goal position\n",
    "- Initial known area\n",
    "- Number of discovered obstacles\n",
    "- Number of replans\n",
    "- Final path length\n",
    "- Actual distance travelled\n",
    "- Number of nodes expanded\n",
    "- Execution time\n",
    "- Whether the goal was reached\n",
    "\n",
    "This experiment can be repeated for different maze sizes to study the effect of maze complexity and partial observation.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 16. Replanning Metrics\n",
    "\n",
    "The following metrics are useful for evaluating reactive navigation:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Metric | Description |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| Replan Count | Number of times the robot calculates a new path |\n",
    "| Final Path Length | Length of the final planned route |\n",
    "| Actual Distance Travelled | Total distance actually travelled by the robot |\n",
    "| Nodes Expanded | Number of search nodes explored during planning |\n",
    "| Execution Time | Time required for navigation and planning |\n",
    "| Discovered Obstacles | Number of previously unknown obstacles detected |\n",
    "| Goal Success | Whether the robot successfully reaches the goal |\n",
    "\n",
    "A useful comparison is between the ideal path obtained from the complete map and the actual distance travelled under partial observation.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 17. Navigation Experiment Pseudocode\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "Initialize ground_truth_map\n",
    "Initialize discovered_map with unknown cells\n",
    "Set robot_position = START\n",
    "\n",
    "while robot_position != GOAL:\n",
    "\n",
    "    Observe surroundings\n",
    "\n",
    "    Update discovered_map\n",
    "\n",
    "    if no current path exists:\n",
    "        Run A* on discovered_map\n",
    "        Store planned path\n",
    "\n",
    "    if newly discovered obstacle affects planned path:\n",
    "        Replan using A*\n",
    "        Increment replan_count\n",
    "\n",
    "    Move robot one step along planned path\n",
    "\n",
    "    Update actual_distance\n",
    "\n",
    "if robot_position == GOAL:\n",
    "    navigation_success = True\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    navigation_success = False"
   ]
