    "\n",
    "| Metric | Result |\n",
    "|---|---:|\n",
    "| Start Position | (0, 0) |\n",
    "| Goal Position | (9, 9) |\n",
    "| Final Robot Position | (9, 9) |\n",
    "| Total A* Plans | 2 |\n",
    "| Replan Count | 1 |\n",
    "| Discovered Obstacles | 1 |\n",
    "| Actual Distance Travelled | 18 |\n",
    "| Navigation Success | True |\n",
    "\n",
    "### Obstacle Discovery\n",
    "\n",
    "During navigation, the robot discovered a previously unknown obstacle at:\n",
    "\n",
    "**(0, 6)**\n",
    "\n",
    "The newly discovered obstacle affected the current planned route. Therefore, the robot triggered replanning using A*.\n",
    "\n",
    "The experiment produced the following navigation sequence:\n",
    "\n",
    "**Initial A* Plan → Obstacle Discovery → Current Path Affected → Replanning → New A* Plan → Goal Reached**\n",
    "\n",
    "### Result Interpretation\n",
    "\n",
    "The experiment demonstrates that Reactive A* can adapt when new obstacle information becomes available during navigation.\n",
    "\n",
    "The robot successfully reached the goal after discovering one previously unknown obstacle and performing one replan.\n",
    "\n",
    "The actual distance travelled was 18 grid movements. In this particular experiment, the discovered obstacle did not increase the final travel distance because an alternative route of the same length was available.\n",
    "\n",
    "The experiment therefore demonstrates that **obstacle discovery and replanning do not necessarily increase path length**, although they can increase the amount of planning performed.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 23. Navigation Findings\n",
    "\n",
    "The experiment provides the following findings:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. The robot can successfully navigate using only progressively discovered information.\n",
    "2. A previously unknown obstacle can be detected during movement.\n",
    "3. When the obstacle affects the current route, Reactive A* triggers replanning.\n",
    "4. The robot required two A* planning operations in total.\n",
    "5. Only one replan was required for the tested scenario.\n",
    "6. The robot successfully reached the goal after replanning.\n",
    "7. The additional planning did not increase the actual travel distance in this particular maze.\n",
    "\n",
    "These findings are specific to the tested 10 × 10 simulation and should not be generalized to all maze configurations.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 24. Conclusion of Member 2 Experiment\n",
    "\n",
    "The Reactive A* demonstration successfully shows the main concept of autonomous navigation under partial observation.\n",
    "\n",
    "The robot starts without complete knowledge of the environment, observes its surroundings, discovers an obstacle, updates its discovered map and replans the route when the current path is affected.\n",
    "\n",
    "This experiment provides an initial validation of the proposed:\n",
    "\n",
    "**Observe → Update → Plan → Move → Discover → Replan → Continue**\n",
    "\n",
    "navigation cycle.\n",
    "\n",
    "Further experiments with different maze sizes, obstacle configurations and observation ranges can be used to study replanning frequency and navigation efficiency in greater detail."
